1 polymer     man 
;Alpha-1B adrenergic receptor,alpha1B adrenergic receptor,Alpha-1B adrenergic receptor,alpha1B adrenergic receptor,Alpha-1B adrenergic receptor,alpha1B adrenergic receptor,Alpha-1B adrenergic receptor,alpha1B adrenergic receptor
;
50442.914 1 ? S95C,I116T,V124M,S150Y,S168C,G183V,D191Y,E194V,T295M,V333L,F334L,P349L ? 
;Residues 38-350 represent the human alpha1B adrenergic receptor, mutant B1 (alpha1B-AR-B1). Residues 249 to 283 were deleted for crystallisation purposes. Residues 351 to 359 form a linker connecting alpha1B-AR-B1 with the DARPin crystallisation chaperone. Residues 360 to 515 represent the DARPin crystallisation chaperone that is related to 5LW2. Residues 516 to 518 represent a short linker connecting the DARPin crystallisation chaperone with the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence. Residues 519 to 524 are part of the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence visible in the electron density.,Residues 38-350 represent the human alpha1B adrenergic receptor, mutant B1 (alpha1B-AR-B1). Residues 249 to 283 were deleted for crystallisation purposes. Residues 351 to 359 form a linker connecting alpha1B-AR-B1 with the DARPin crystallisation chaperone. Residues 360 to 515 represent the DARPin crystallisation chaperone that is related to 5LW2. Residues 516 to 518 represent a short linker connecting the DARPin crystallisation chaperone with the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence. Residues 519 to 524 are part of the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence visible in the electron density.,Residues 38-350 represent the human alpha1B adrenergic receptor, mutant B1 (alpha1B-AR-B1). Residues 249 to 283 were deleted for crystallisation purposes. Residues 351 to 359 form a linker connecting alpha1B-AR-B1 with the DARPin crystallisation chaperone. Residues 360 to 515 represent the DARPin crystallisation chaperone that is related to 5LW2. Residues 516 to 518 represent a short linker connecting the DARPin crystallisation chaperone with the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence. Residues 519 to 524 are part of the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence visible in the electron density.,Residues 38-350 represent the human alpha1B adrenergic receptor, mutant B1 (alpha1B-AR-B1). Residues 249 to 283 were deleted for crystallisation purposes. Residues 351 to 359 form a linker connecting alpha1B-AR-B1 with the DARPin crystallisation chaperone. Residues 360 to 515 represent the DARPin crystallisation chaperone that is related to 5LW2. Residues 516 to 518 represent a short linker connecting the DARPin crystallisation chaperone with the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence. Residues 519 to 524 are part of the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence visible in the electron density.,Residues 38-350 represent the human alpha1B adrenergic receptor, mutant B1 (alpha1B-AR-B1). Residues 249 to 283 were deleted for crystallisation purposes. Residues 351 to 359 form a linker connecting alpha1B-AR-B1 with the DARPin crystallisation chaperone. Residues 360 to 515 represent the DARPin crystallisation chaperone that is related to 5LW2. Residues 516 to 518 represent a short linker connecting the DARPin crystallisation chaperone with the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence. Residues 519 to 524 are part of the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence visible in the electron density.,Residues 38-350 represent the human alpha1B adrenergic receptor, mutant B1 (alpha1B-AR-B1). Residues 249 to 283 were deleted for crystallisation purposes. Residues 351 to 359 form a linker connecting alpha1B-AR-B1 with the DARPin crystallisation chaperone. Residues 360 to 515 represent the DARPin crystallisation chaperone that is related to 5LW2. Residues 516 to 518 represent a short linker connecting the DARPin crystallisation chaperone with the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence. Residues 519 to 524 are part of the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence visible in the electron density.,Residues 38-350 represent the human alpha1B adrenergic receptor, mutant B1 (alpha1B-AR-B1). Residues 249 to 283 were deleted for crystallisation purposes. Residues 351 to 359 form a linker connecting alpha1B-AR-B1 with the DARPin crystallisation chaperone. Residues 360 to 515 represent the DARPin crystallisation chaperone that is related to 5LW2. Residues 516 to 518 represent a short linker connecting the DARPin crystallisation chaperone with the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence. Residues 519 to 524 are part of the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence visible in the electron density.,Residues 38-350 represent the human alpha1B adrenergic receptor, mutant B1 (alpha1B-AR-B1). Residues 249 to 283 were deleted for crystallisation purposes. Residues 351 to 359 form a linker connecting alpha1B-AR-B1 with the DARPin crystallisation chaperone. Residues 360 to 515 represent the DARPin crystallisation chaperone that is related to 5LW2. Residues 516 to 518 represent a short linker connecting the DARPin crystallisation chaperone with the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence. Residues 519 to 524 are part of the HRV 3C protease recognition sequence visible in the electron density.
